# BMAD-generated content — installer output from `bmad install`.
# Keep byte-identical to what the installer produces so re-running it yields no
# spurious diff. Never reformat these. Team/personal config in _bmad/custom/ and
# your own (non-bmad-) skills/agents are NOT ignored and format normally.
_bmad/
.claude/skills/bmad-*/
.agents/skills/bmad-*/
.github/agents/bmad-*
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Written by `expo prebuild` back into the tracked source tree.
# @bacons/apple-targets' watch-icon mod writes this file itself, via
# writeContentsJsonAsync -> JSON.stringify(…, null, 2) with NO trailing newline
# (@expo/prebuild-config/build/plugins/icons/AssetContents.js). Prettier wants to
# add that newline. The two can never agree, so whichever tool writes last, the
# other reports the file as modified -- which is why `yarn watch:prebuild` used to
# leave a stray one-byte diff in `git status` for a file nobody touched.
# prebuild is the generator of record here, so keep prettier (and, via this file,
# lint-staged) out of it and let the tracked bytes match prebuild exactly.
targets/watch/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/Contents.json

# Hand-tuned HTML, deliberately left as authored.
# docs/ is served publicly by GitHub Pages (https://ifero.github.io/myLoyaltyCards/,
# source main:/docs) and supabase/templates/ are the transactional auth emails.
# Prettier's HTML printer explodes every inline style="…" attribute across multiple
# lines and reflows inline elements: ~1.2k lines of churn, no functional gain, and
# multi-line attributes are exactly what older email clients mishandle. All risk,
# no upside. Sibling CSS is NOT ignored -- prettier's CSS output is safe.
docs/*.html
supabase/templates/*.html
